{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/100283","id":2229397678,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6E4eiu","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100283","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100283.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100283.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100283","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/100283/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/100283/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100283/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/3b70fbdc3cd0fea0e8c3de193ab6c8db2d37049b","number":100283,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Implement motion vectors in mobile renderer","user":{"login":"devloglogan","id":95497005,"node_id":"U_kgDOBbErLQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/95497005?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/devloglogan","html_url":"https://github.com/devloglogan","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/devloglogan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/devloglogan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/devloglogan/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/devloglogan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/devloglogan/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/devloglogan/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/devloglogan/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/devloglogan/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/devloglogan/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"This is the mobile renderer implementation of motion vectors, built on top of the renderer-agnostic https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100282. A fair amount of discussion related to motion vectors has taken place in the compatibility renderer version of this PR: https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/97151.\r\n\r\nIf you'd like to test this PR out, build the OpenXR vendor repo with the PR adding support for `XR_FB_space_warp`: https://github.com/GodotVR/godot_openxr_vendors/pull/222\r\n\r\n### Technical details ###\r\n\r\nSince the forward+ renderer already implements motion vectors, the additions needed to get them working in the mobile renderer were pretty minimal. The biggest change is updating the vertex shader code of `scene_forward_mobile.glsl`, abstracting it into the `_unpack_vertex_attributes()`/`vertex_shader()` functions, similar to the forward+ renderer.\r\n\r\nMotion vectors are rendered in a new, separate render pass. Here are the reasons for this (copied from https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/97151):\r\n\r\n- Since motion vectors can be rendered at a much smaller resolution this extra pass should be quite fast (e.g. the Quest 3 recommends a resolution of around 420x420).\r\n- This will make it easier to allow developers to include or exclude specific objects from motion vectors, which can be helpful in minimizing the artifacts from space warp. (Note: this isn’t part of the current PR, but something planned for the future.)\r\n- Combining motion vectors with the color pass would hinder future compatibility between Application Space Warp and the XR_META_recommended_layer_resolution OpenXR extension, since all attachments would then have to be of the same resolution.\r\n\r\n### Issues that need to be addressed ###\r\n\r\n- In abstracting the vertex shader code into the `vertex_shader()` function, the new function seems unable to take an argument of type `SceneData`. Whenever trying to do this, the shader breaks and I receive `VK_ERROR_UNKNOWN`. To work around this, I am instead passing all of the needed, individual fields from the `SceneData` structs. This makes for a very long function signature and I'd like to change it if possible.\r\n\r\n- In `scene_forward_mobile.glsl`, the y values of `prev_screen_position`/`screen_position` need to be flipped, but they need to be flipped _after_ they are passed to `gl_Position` in the vertex shader. Without flipping them, the color output of the motion vectors texture is incorrect. But if y is flipped earlier, the position is incorrect. Currently this is solved by flipping the y at the end of the fragment shader when calculating ndc coordinates, but this feels a bit hacky to me. Does anyone have ideas on how else this could be accomplished?\r\n\r\nThis PR will remain as a draft until the other PR it builds upon (https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100282) is merged.\r\n\r\nCloses https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/67606","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098111,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgxMTE=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:rendering","name":"topic:rendering","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":865585000,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw4NjU1ODUwMDA=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:xr","name":"topic:xr","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":12070367,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4AuC3f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/22","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/22","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/22/labels","number":22,"state":"closed","title":"4.5","description":"","creator":{"login":"Sauermann","id":6299227,